WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.714 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Could subtracting two large numbers be easier than adding
two small ones?

00:00:05.364 --> 00:00:09.385 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Today we are choosing mental addition and subtraction
strategies.

00:00:09.605 --> 00:00:16.214 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
We will look at how close the numbers are, try a friendly
number, and explain why our shortcuts keep the answer
correct.

00:00:16.864 --> 00:00:22.337 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Our learning goal is to choose and explain efficient mental
addition and subtraction strategies.

00:00:22.987 --> 00:00:24.744 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Success criteria.

00:00:24.964 --> 00:00:27.769 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can choose counting up for nearby numbers.

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:31.338 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can use a friendly number and undo the adjustment.

00:00:31.558 --> 00:00:34.872 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
I can check an answer using the inverse operation.

00:00:35.522 --> 00:00:38.041 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
A useful strategy fits the numbers.

00:00:38.261 --> 00:00:41.643 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Counting up finds the distance between nearby numbers.

00:00:41.863 --> 00:00:48.015 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Compensation changes a number to make a calculation easier,
then adjusts the answer to undo that change.

00:00:48.665 --> 00:00:53.556 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Find six thousand and four minus five thousand nine hundred
and ninety-seven.

00:00:53.776 --> 00:00:56.407 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Counting up avoids lots of regrouping.

00:00:56.627 --> 00:00:59.113 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
First go up three to six thousand.

00:00:59.763 --> 00:01:01.488 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Then go up four more.

00:01:01.708 --> 00:01:05.223 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The total distance is three plus four, which is seven.

00:01:05.443 --> 00:01:10.582 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Check: five thousand nine hundred and ninety-seven plus
seven is six thousand and four.

00:01:11.232 --> 00:01:15.475 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Now add three hundred and ninety-eight and two hundred and
fifty-seven.

00:01:15.695 --> 00:01:18.965 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Move the first number up by two to make four hundred.

00:01:19.615 --> 00:01:24.128 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
We added two too many, so subtract two from six hundred and
fifty-seven.

00:01:24.348 --> 00:01:27.232 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The answer is six hundred and fifty-five.

00:01:27.452 --> 00:01:31.869 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Compensation preserves the original total after we undo the
change.

00:01:32.519 --> 00:01:38.262 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
An easy mix-up is adding two again after changing three
hundred and ninety-eight to four hundred.

00:01:38.482 --> 00:01:42.963 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The friendly calculation is already two too high, so
subtract two.

00:01:43.309 --> 00:01:46.413 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
You can check by returning to the original numbers.

00:01:47.063 --> 00:01:50.749 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Try five hundred and two minus four hundred and
ninety-eight.

00:01:50.969 --> 00:01:52.399 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Can you count up?

00:01:56.399 --> 00:02:00.313 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Go up two to five hundred, then two more to five hundred and
two.

00:02:00.533 --> 00:02:02.299 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
The difference is four.

00:02:02.949 --> 00:02:05.642 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Look at the numbers before choosing a method.

00:02:05.862 --> 00:02:10.468 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Use counting up for nearby numbers and compensation for
friendly totals.

00:02:10.688 --> 00:02:14.918 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Explain the adjustment and check using the inverse
operation.

00:02:15.138 --> 00:02:18.297 line:0% position:50% align:center size:96%
Now choose a strategy and explain why it works.
